---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro';
import { BRAND_NAME } from '~/lib/site';
---

<Base
  title={`Privacy & Cookie Policy | ${BRAND_NAME}`}
  description="What data this site collects, which cookies it sets, and how to opt out."
>
  <div class="wrap prose page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
    <p>
      We collect as little as possible. This site is a static publication — it
      has no accounts, no forms that store personal data, and no server-side
      tracking of our own.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and consent</h2>
    <p>
      On your first visit we ask for consent before loading anything that sets
      cookies. If you <strong>decline</strong>, no advertising or Google
      Analytics cookies are set. If you <strong>accept</strong>, the following
      third parties may set cookies:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google AdSense</strong> — serves display ads and may use
        cookies to personalize them. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Google's advertising policies</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — anonymized usage statistics
        (which pages are read, roughly where from). IP anonymization is
        enabled.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> runs regardless of consent —
      it is cookieless and collects no personal data.
    </p>

    <h2>Changing your mind</h2>
    <p>
      Clear this site's data in your browser (localStorage and cookies) and
      the consent banner will ask again on your next visit.
    </p>

    <h2>Ad personalization</h2>
    <p>
      You can opt out of Google ad personalization at
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">adssettings.google.com</a>.
      Users in the EEA/UK are shown Google's consent flow as required.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Privacy questions: see the contact details on our
      <a href="/about/">about page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 2rem;
  }
</style>
